    roads: "No roads: LRV tracks are paired 23 cm-wide bands with chevron tread imprints, 1.8 m track gauge, slightly darker than the undisturbed surface (compacted, fresh subsurface fines) with small rooster-tail spray marks; they wind around craters and boulders.",
    kerbsPavements: "None.",
    pathsAlleys: "Astronaut 'paths': trampled bands of boot prints between LM, LRV and ALSEP, darker and rougher than surroundings.",
    squaresCourtyards: "LM site and ALSEP field: a roughly 100 m patch of disturbed, darker, footprint-covered regolith, blast-scoured zone around the LM (lighter, swept smooth radially).",
    shore: "No water. Regolith colour: neutral grey #8a8a88 in flat light, darker #5f5f5d at low phase/disturbed soil, the orange glass soil at Shorty crater (#9a6a45) is the one colour accent; massif slopes lighter grey-tan #b2aca2; many small craters, rocks and boulders with fillets.",
    notes: "Hard black shadows, black sky, no atmospheric haze; regolith is fine-grained and uniform, not sandy dunes. Tracks and footprints keep sharp edges.",
